    "knowledge_point": "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function",
    "problem": "The function $P(t)=710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})$ represents the volume of milk, in liters, produced on a farm $t$ days after the owner bought new cows. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk as a function of $t?$",
    "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk with respect to time is ${P}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $P(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})) \\\\  & =710\\,\\frac{{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk is  $\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$ liters per day.",
